\section{Keeping a lazy table}{

A lazy table is a live connection to a file on disk, not data. It cannot be
saved with \code{\link[=saveRDS]{saveRDS()}} and reloaded in another session --- doing so gives you
an object that errors with \verb{Invalid connection}. This is how dplyr behaves
against every database backend. To keep results across sessions, either
\code{\link[dplyr:collect]{dplyr::collect()}} the table into a tibble first, or use \code{as = "path"} and
